Falsifies `capability::delegation_needs_grant_and_never_widens`.

The defect: the `GRANT` check dropped from `Capability::delegate`, so a capability whose
holder was never trusted to lend it is lent anyway, narrowed or not. This is the rule the
crate's own documentation gives `GRANT` and the kernel's delegation applies.

Expected to fail: `assert_ne!(source.rights.0 & GRANT_BIT, 0)` in the `Ok` arm, on a source
without the `GRANT` bit and a request inside it.

diff --git a/crates/capability/src/lib.rs b/crates/capability/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/capability/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/capability/src/lib.rs
@@ -140,9 +140,6 @@
     ///
     /// Name: provisional (`delegate`, `GrantRequired`).
     pub fn delegate(&self, rights: Rights) -> Result<Capability<O>, Error> {
-        if !self.rights.allows(Rights::GRANT) {
-            return Err(Error::GrantRequired);
-        }
         if !rights.is_subset_of(self.rights) {
             return Err(Error::CannotWiden);
         }
